      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As an AI, I cannot issue definitive legal rulings on the constitutionality of specific laws, as that requires a judge applying the law to facts in a specific case. While the *Bruen* standard makes the constitutional viability of modern restrictions much harder to prove, the final determination rests on whether the regulating body and courts successfully map a historical tradition onto the modern statute. Therefore, the legal conclusion is not automatically conclusive without that judicial step.",
      "source": "target",
